---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../components/ProjectCard.astro';
---

<Layout title="Scott Okamoto - Portfolio">
  <section id="home" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="text-center pt-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3 tracking-tight">
        Scott Okamoto
      </h1>

      <p class="text-accent-blue text-sm font-medium tracking-wide uppercase">
        Full-Stack Developer
      </p>

      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-6 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-lg leading-relaxed">
        I build real-time and full-stack web applications designed for performance, reliability, and seamless user interaction.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 mt-8 justify-center">
        <a href="#projects"
          class="bg-accent-blue hover:bg-blue-400 text-black font-medium px-6 py-3 rounded-lg transition-all duration-200 hover:shadow-[0_0_12px_theme(colors.accent.blue/25%)] text-center sm:min-w-[140px]">
          View Projects
        </a>
        <a href="#contact"
          class="text-accent-blue hover:text-blue-400 border border-border-subtle hover:border-accent-blue px-6 py-3 rounded-lg transition-all duration-200 text-center sm:min-w-[140px]">
          Contact
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="about" class="bg-bg-surface max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-8 text-center">
      About
    </h2>
    <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle rounded-2xl p-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <div class="space-y-4 text-text-secondary leading-relaxed text-center">
        <p>
          I transitioned into software development through a web development bootcamp and have been focused on building backend-driven applications since.
        </p>

        <p>
          I primarily work with <span class="text-accent-blue font-medium">TypeScript and Node.js</span>, building full-stack applications with an emphasis on real-time systems and interactive user experiences.
        </p>

        <p>
          I also have experience with Python and Go, and I’m drawn to problems involving shared state, synchronization, and real-time interaction.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="projects" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-8 text-center">
      Projects
    </h2>
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-2">
      <ProjectCard 
        title="Relay RPG"
        description="A play-by-post storytelling Discord bot where small groups collaboratively write stories driven by dice mechanics. Players create persistent characters, join story hooks posted to a shared board, and take turns building narrative — each roll shaping what the next player inherits."
        tech={["Node.js", "SQLite", "Discord SDK", "Fly.io"]}
        github="https://github.com/swokamoto/relay-rpg"
      />
      <ProjectCard 
        title="Isabelle's Bead Shop"
        description="Full-stack e-commerce platform with admin dashboard for inventory management and customer reviews. Secure checkout process with Stripe integration and responsive product catalog."
        tech={["React", "Node.js", "Stripe", "MongoDB"]}
        github="https://github.com/hannah-finch/isabelles-bead-shop"
        live="https://isabellesbeadshop.onrender.com/"
      />
      <ProjectCard 
        title="Zen Garden"
        description="Full-stack garden planner where users design and customize their own plot by placing trees, bushes, and flowers rendered in real-time with animated SVG graphics. Features user authentication, persistent plot data, and a REST API backend."
        tech={["Handlebars", "SVG", "PostgreSQL", "Sequelize"]}
        github="https://github.com/swokamoto/zenGarden2"
        live="https://zengarden-5q63.onrender.com/"
      />
      <ProjectCard 
        title="PokeLounge"
        description="Interactive ambient web app where users add up to 4 Pokémon to a cozy scene via the PokéAPI, drag-and-drop them between seats, and relax to a built-in lofi music player. Pokémon selections persist across sessions via localStorage, scenes are swappable, and each Pokémon generates a Chuck Norris joke with their name swapped in via a second API."
        tech={["JQuery", "JavaScript", "HTML", "CSS"]}
        github="https://github.com/swokamoto/group-11-project-pokemon"
        live="https://group11projectpokemon.github.io/group-11-project-pokemon/"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="process" class="bg-bg-surface max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-8 text-center">
      How I Build
    </h2>
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle p-6 rounded-lg hover:border-accent-blue transition-all duration-200">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-2">Structure First</h3>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Plan user flows before writing code. In Relay RPG, I mapped the full turn sequence and shared board logic before touching the Discord SDK, which kept the data model clean and the command handlers predictable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle p-6 rounded-lg hover:border-accent-blue transition-all duration-200">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-2">Real-Time First</h3>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Built Zen Garden's SVG rendering to update instantly on user interaction without page reloads, using a REST API backend to persist state between sessions. Relay RPG similarly tracks turn state across multiple concurrent players.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle p-6 rounded-lg hover:border-accent-blue transition-all duration-200">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-2">API Design</h3>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Design backend routes around the data the frontend actually needs. Isabelle's Bead Shop uses a clear separation between the customer-facing catalog API and the admin inventory endpoints, with Stripe webhooks handled server-side.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle p-6 rounded-lg hover:border-accent-blue transition-all duration-200">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-text-primary mb-2">Error Handling</h3>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm leading-relaxed">Build for failure cases early. PokeLounge falls back gracefully when the PokéAPI or Chuck Norris API is slow or unavailable, and localStorage keeps Pokémon selections intact across sessions without requiring a backend.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-8 text-center">
      Contact
    </h2>
    <div class="bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle rounded-2xl p-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-text-secondary text-center mb-6">
        Open to full-time and contract opportunities in full-stack development.
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-6">
          <span class="text-text-muted text-sm">Email</span>
          <a href="mailto:swokamoto@gmail.com" class="text-accent-blue hover:text-blue-400 transition-all duration-200">swokamoto@gmail.com</a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-6">
          <span class="text-text-muted text-sm">LinkedIn</span>
          <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/sokamoto" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-accent-blue hover:text-blue-400 transition-all duration-200">linkedin.com/in/scott-okamoto</a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-6">
          <span class="text-text-muted text-sm">GitHub</span>
          <a href="https://github.com/swokamoto" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-accent-blue hover:text-blue-400 transition-all duration-200">github.com/swokamoto</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>